WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.170
After years away from theaters, the Blade
franchise is coming back - but it has a new

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.170
leading man.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.950
Why did Marvel decide to go with Mahershala
Ali as its new Blade instead of sticking with

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.049
Wesley Snipes?

00:00:10.049 --> 00:00:14.320
While we wait for the character's Phase 5
MCU revival, here's everything we know.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.160
By August of 2019, Wesley Snipes will be 57
years old.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.890
Granted, Snipes has aged well and we're willing
to bet the guy who gave us the martial arts

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.880
moves we saw in his many action flicks can
still throw a mean kick.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.680
Also, age is meaning less and less these days
when it comes to casting.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.660
Harrison Ford was 65 when Indiana Jones and
the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull was released

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.730
in theaters, and even though he's now in his
late 70s, he'll return to the role again in

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.070
Indiana Jones 5.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.900
Not to mention the impressive advances in
de-aging technology – something Marvel Studios

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.280
has already used successfully a number of
times to impressive results.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.240
"Do me a favor?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.320
Try not to burn the house down before Monday?"

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.680
"OK, so it's Monday.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.680
That is good to know.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.510
I will plan my toga party accordingly."

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.560
But there are differences between those examples
and the potential of casting Snipes as Blade

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.179
- the most glaring issue being that Blade's
part vampire.

00:01:01.179 --> 00:01:04.449
A 77-year-old can play Indiana Jones because
Indy's human.

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:08.030
In the first Blade film series, it's established
Blade ages normally.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.860
But in the comics, while Blade isn't immortal
like full vampires, he ages slower than humans.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.570
The new Blade films may be closer to the comics
in this way.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:20.520
If so, having a 57-year-old half-vampire who
looks like he's 57 doesn't work.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.640
Largely thanks to a 2012 A.V.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.630
Club interview with Patton Oswalt about his
most memorable roles, Wesley Snipes' supposed

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.080
behavior on the set of Blade: Trinity has
become absolutely, hilariously infamous.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.440
"If you sit and watch Blade Trinity, it's
a D-.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.850
It just doesn't work.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:40.320
But if you know what they went through to
get that movie made… it is an A."

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.920
Snipes and Trinity director David Goyer didn't
get along behind the camera.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.810
According to Oswalt, Snipes accused Goyer
of racism and at one point sat down with the

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.460
director and tried to convince him to quit,
only to have Goyer retort that since they'd

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.130
already filmed all of Snipes' close-ups and
could use a stand-in for everything else,

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.390
Snipes should quit instead.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:00.829
Oswalt said after that confrontation, Snipes
refused to communicate with Goyer directly.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:05.939
"After a while, he resorted to just - he would
communicate with Post-Its that he would give

00:02:05.939 --> 00:02:09.760
to the director… and each one he would sign
'Blade.'"

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Blade: Trinity came out well over a decade
ago, and it could be that Snipes has mellowed

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.070
with age.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:19.690
Regardless, Marvel will probably try to recruit
some impressive directorial talent for their

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:23.520
new Blade film, and doing that will probably
be easier without a lead actor you can't even

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.520
get to use his words.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.840
"Come on - use your words, buddy."

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.600
It could be that any concern about Wesley
Snipes returning to play Blade is baseless

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.600
- but that still doesn't change the reality
that we got to see Snipes play Blade in three

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:34.600
films.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.200
Bringing him back to the role would waste
the marvelous opportunity of finding a new

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.410
actor to give us a different shade of Blade.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.530
Mahershala Ali is a tremendous catch.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.090
We don't know much about the film yet, including
its release date, but we know plenty about

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.130
Ali's talent.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.080
He's got two Academy Awards for Best Actor
in a Supporting Role under his belt - one

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.920
for 2017's Moonlight and another for 2019's
Green Book.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.060
He's brilliant as political consultant Remy
Danton in House of Cards, as well as the villain

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.560
Cottonmouth in the first season of Luke Cage.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.480
Any Marvel fan, any Blade fan, or just any
person with even slightly good taste should

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.560
be thrilled about the casting.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.820
"It looks like you brought your own hat, Mahershala.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.820
You did?

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:11.820
What is that?"

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.810
Just because Wesley Snipes won't be returning
as Blade doesn't mean he won't be in the film.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.730
When it comes to paying tribute to writers,
artists, and actors, Marvel Studios has a

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.970
fine track record, and there's no reason Snipes
couldn't fill another role in the upcoming

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.970
Blade.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.250
One perfect choice could be the role of Whistler
- Blade's mentor-slash-father figure.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:34.700
Kris Kristofferson played Whistler in the
original film trilogy, and Snipes could be

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.880
perfect casting for the rebooted character.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.760
"How do you feel."

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.760
"Like hammered s---."

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.930
We're not the first ones to have the idea.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:52.660
Immediately following the news of Ali's casting
as the new Blade, Snipes fans reacted quickly.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.900
Many accepted the new casting but with the
preference that they wanted Snipes in the

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.730
film in some capacity, even if it was just
a cameo, and more than a few fans named Whistler

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.310
as a perfect fit.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:06.180
Since we know Snipes talked to Marvel about
something, this may already be in the works.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.460
In a couple of years we could see Snipes yelling
at Ali for saving vampire-bite survivors and

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.080
chain-smoking while spilling gasoline all
over the place.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.230
Whatever his reputation for on-set shenanigans
might be, you've got to give Wesley Snipes

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:21.730
this much: After the news broke that Marvel
had hired Mahershala Ali to play the rebooted

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.090
Blade, the O.G.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.760
Daywalker took it publicly in stride, waiting
a few days for things to settle down before

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.260
talking to the press and assuring his fans
that he supports the studio's decision.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.700
Snipes addressed his fans in a statement,
writing, in part:

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:37.060
"To all the DAYWALKERS losing their minds
right now, chillaaxx.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.790
Although the news comes as a surprise, it's
ALL good.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.620
Such is the 'business' of 'entertainment!'

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.190
Much peace to the MCU crew - always a fan.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:48.290
[…] Congratulations and Salaam to Mahershala
Ali, a beautiful and talented artist whose

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.540
expressions I look forward to experiencing
for many years to come."

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:55.190
Whether Snipes' magnanimous reaction stems
from a secret involvement in the new Blade

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.820
or simply some good old-fashioned maturity
is anyone's guess at this point.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.290
Either way, it looks like everyone's happy
with the way the future of the franchise is

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.930
shaping up - even if the man who originally
brought the central character to life has

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.200
ended up losing the role in the process.

